<!--   ==== Exemple of a DRT line with stops (French Profile)  ======
 
Overview 
=======
The Line XYZ starts at a regular stop "A" (a train station for exemple), the covers a DRT area "Z" that contains multiple bus stops 
grouped together in small zones ("Z1 and "Z2"). Z1 contains bus stops (Quays) B, C and D; Z2 contains bus stops E, F, G.  
The small zones are used to provide better theorical departure / arrival times than 
having only one time for all de "Z" zone, and to enable RoutingConstraintZone for small zones (passengers cannot travel from one point 
of a small zone to an other).

This exemple contains reservations information : passengers car board on "A" without reservation, only telling 
the driver at what stop they want to go. For other stop (in the "Z" zone), reservation has to be made 2 hours before departure or 
the day before if the departure is before 8h30.

Modelization
============

Based on French profile, but including all files into one global CompositeFrame.

- There is only one Route, with 2 RoutePoints : 
    - RoutePoint A
    - RoutePoint Z
- There is 2 ServiceJourneyPattern with 3 StopPointInJourneyPattern (SPiJP)
    - SPiJP A, referencing a ScheduledStopPoint SSP-A
    - SPiJP Z1, referencing a ScheduledStopPoint SSP-Z1, and RoutePointZ (in FlexiblePointProperties)
    - SPiJP Z2, referencing a ScheduledStopPoint SSP-Z2, and RoutePointZ (in FlexiblePointProperties)
- There is 2 ServiceJourney with 3 TimetabledPassingTime and PassengerAtStopTime
    - referencing SPiJP A 
    - referencing SPiJP Z1
    - referencing SPiJP Z2

Other associations :
- 2 FlexibleStopAssignement associates SSP-Z1 and SSP-Z2 with the corresponding FlexibleStopPlaces (FSP-Z1 and FSP-Z2)
- 2 FlexibleStopPlaces includes FlexibleArea, containing de SSPs ([SSP-Z1-B,SSP-Z1-C, SSP-Z1-D] and [SSP-Z2-E, SSP-Z2-F, SSP-Z2-G]) 
- RoutingConstraintZones have references to all the SSP of a small zone (Z1 or Z2)
- PassengerStopAssignements make associations to SSP to Quays 

Questions
=========
- about RoutePoints : 
    - What is the use of RoutePoints in regular lines as RoutePoint can only be referenced by FlexiblePointProperties ?
    - Some NeTEx exemples are using "ScheduledStopPoint" in PointOnRoute instead of RoutePoint. It is valid because PointOnRoute 
        expects a Point, but is it a good practice ? Point is highly abstract object.
- about ScheduledStopPoints : 
    - They are used in 2 different ways, as "point" and "zones" in SPiJP, and as "points" in FlexibleStopPlace
    - If a consumer wants to collect the Quays from the Route level (for map display) :
        - Regular RoutePoints are not associated with Quays => impossible (or use SSP instead of RoutePoint)
        - DRT RoutePOints : RoutePoint <- SPiJP -> SSP (zone) <- FlexibleStopAssignement -> FlexibleStopPlace -> FlexibleStopArea -> SSP (point) <- PassengerStopAssignement -> Quay and StopPlace
              
-->
